Rem ===================================================================
Rem tests/test-tables.shoddy -- what must be true of the cave itself.
Rem
Rem   ./build.sh test     (runs this and the rest of tests/)
Rem
Rem These checks need no oracle. Every one of them asserts something that
Rem has to hold of any correct build -- a travel row cannot name a room
Rem that does not exist, a block of travel rules has to end in a row with
Rem Stop set or the scan runs off the table, a hint has to cost points --
Rem so they are worth exactly as much on a machine with no reference
Rem transcripts as on one with them.
Rem
Rem That is the point. The port's tables used to be produced by a
Rem generator from YAML and are now hand-edited Shoddy, which trades one
Rem risk for another: no generator can silently drop a field, but a
Rem person can. This file is what replaced the generator's guarantees.
Rem ===================================================================

Include "harness.shoddy"

Rem ---- the travel table ------------------------------------------------
Rem 878 rows, each a motion word, a condition, and somewhere to end up.
Rem The indices in them are the whole risk: they are plain numbers, and a
Rem wrong one is a room you have never heard of, or an abort.

Def NRooms() As Number
    Length(Locations())

Def NMessages() As Number
    Length(Messages())

Def NRows() As Number
    Length(Travels())

Rem A destination is one of three things, and each has its own range.
Rem The three specials are hardcoded passages in the rules, numbered from
Rem one, so a fourth would be a rule nobody wrote.
Def DestOk(o As Op) As Boolean
    Select Case Destination(o)
        Case ToRoom(r)
            r >= 0 And r < NRooms()
        Case ToMessage(m)
            m >= 0 And m < NMessages()
        Case ToSpecial(s)
            s >= 1 And s <= 3

Def CheckTravelRows()
    Rem every destination lands somewhere that exists
    Assert(All(Range(0, NRows() - 1), Fn(i) => DestOk(RowAt(i))),
           "EVERY TRAVEL ROW LEADS SOMEWHERE THAT EXISTS")

    Rem every motion word on a row is a word the parser can produce
    Assert(All(Range(0, NRows() - 1),
           Fn(i) => Motion(RowAt(i)) >= 0 And Motion(RowAt(i)) < Length(Motions())),
           "EVERY TRAVEL ROW NAMES A REAL MOTION WORD")

    Rem a Chance percentage is a percentage
    Assert(All(Range(0, NRows() - 1), Fn(i) => PctOk(RowAt(i))),
           "EVERY CHANCE CONDITION IS A PERCENTAGE")

    Rem a condition that names an object names one that exists
    Assert(All(Range(0, NRows() - 1), Fn(i) => CondObjOk(RowAt(i))),
           "EVERY TRAVEL CONDITION NAMES A REAL OBJECT")

Def PctOk(o As Op) As Boolean
    Select Case Condition(o)
        Case Chance(p)
            p >= 0 And p <= 100
        Case Else
            True

Def CondObjOk(o As Op) As Boolean
    Select Case Condition(o)
        Case Carrying(obj)
            ObjIndexOk(obj)
        Case CarriedOrHere(obj)
            ObjIndexOk(obj)
        Case NotInState(obj, st)
            ObjIndexOk(obj)
        Case Else
            True

Def ObjIndexOk(i As Number) As Boolean
    i >= 0 And i < Length(Objects())

Rem ---- the travel blocks -----------------------------------------------
Rem Tkey(loc) is where a room's rules start; the scan walks forward until
Rem a row with Stop set. A block whose last row has no Stop would run the
Rem scan into the next room's rules and then off the end of the table --
Rem which is a hang or an abort, never a wrong answer, so nothing milder
Rem than this check would find it.

Def BlockEnds(i As Number) As Boolean
    If i >= NRows() Then
        False
    Else
        If Stop(RowAt(i)) Then
            True
        Else
            BlockEnds(i + 1)

Def CheckTravelBlocks()
    Assert(All(Range(1, NRooms()),
           Fn(i) => Nth(Tkey(), i) >= 0 And Nth(Tkey(), i) < NRows()),
           "EVERY TRAVEL KEY IS A ROW INDEX")

    Assert(All(Range(1, NRooms()),
           Fn(i) => Nth(Tkey(), i) = 0 Or BlockEnds(Nth(Tkey(), i))),
           "EVERY BLOCK OF TRAVEL RULES ENDS IN A STOP ROW")

Rem ---- the rooms -------------------------------------------------------

Rem The flags a room may carry. The rules ask about these by name, so a
Rem typo in the data is a flag that is simply never true -- a room that
Rem is quietly never dark, or never deep enough for the curmudgeons to
Rem walk into. Nothing at runtime would complain.
Def KnownConds() As List Of String
    { "ABOVE", "ALLALIKE", "ALLDIFFERENT", "DEEP", "FLUID",
      "FOREST", "LIT", "NOARRR", "NOBACK", "OILY" }

Def RoomCondsOk(r As Room) As Boolean
    All(Conds(r), Fn(c) => Contains(KnownConds(), c))

Def CheckRooms()
    Assert(All(Range(1, NRooms()), Fn(i) => RoomCondsOk(Nth(Locations(), i))),
           "EVERY ROOM FLAG IS ONE THE RULES KNOW")

    Rem -1 is silence; anything else indexes the message table
    Assert(All(Range(1, NRooms()),
           Fn(i) => Noise(Nth(Locations(), i)) = 0 - 1
                            Or (Noise(Nth(Locations(), i)) >= 0
                                And Noise(Nth(Locations(), i)) < NMessages())),
           "EVERY ROOM SOUND IS SILENCE OR A REAL MESSAGE")

    Assert(All(Range(1, NRooms()),
           Fn(i) => All(RoomHints(Nth(Locations(), i)),
                                Fn(h) => h >= 0 And h < Length(Hints()))),
           "EVERY ROOM HINT IS A REAL HINT")

    Rem A room with no long description prints nothing on arrival, which
    Rem is a bug everywhere except in a forced room -- one whose travel
    Rem block begins with the magic HERE motion, so you are moved straight
    Rem on again and never stand in it. LOC_BUILDING1 is the only one that
    Rem takes the exemption: it is the moment of climbing the beanstalk,
    Rem and which room it forwards you to depends on how tall the plant is.
    Assert(All(Range(2, NRooms()),
           Fn(i) => ForcedAt(i - 1) Or Len(Long(Nth(Locations(), i))) > 0),
           "EVERY ROOM YOU CAN STAND IN DESCRIBES ITSELF")

    Rem and the exemption is not a licence: a forced room has to lead
    Rem somewhere, or it is a room the game cannot get you out of
    Assert(All(Range(2, NRooms()),
           Fn(i) => Not ForcedAt(i - 1) Or LeadsToARoom(Nth(Tkey(), i))),
           "EVERY FORCED ROOM FORWARDS YOU TO A REAL ROOM")

Def LeadsToARoom(k As Number) As Boolean
    If k = 0 Then
        False
    Else
        If GoesTo(RowAt(k)) <> NoRoom() Then
            True
        Else
            If Stop(RowAt(k)) Then
                False
            Else
                LeadsToARoom(k + 1)

Rem ---- the objects -----------------------------------------------------

Def CheckObjects()
    Assert(All(Range(1, Length(Objects())),
           Fn(i) => All(Places(Nth(Objects(), i)),
                                Fn(p) => p >= 0 And p < NRooms())),
           "EVERY OBJECT STARTS IN A REAL ROOM")

    Rem An object's prop indexes its description list, so a thing with
    Rem states needs a description for each of them or a state change
    Rem describes nothing.
    Assert(All(Range(1, Length(Objects())), Fn(i) => StateArityOk(Nth(Objects(), i))),
           "EVERY OBJECT WITH STATES CAN DESCRIBE EACH OF THEM")

    Rem two rooms at most: the grate seen from above and below, the troll
    Rem at both ends of its bridge
    Assert(All(Range(1, Length(Objects())),
           Fn(i) => Length(Places(Nth(Objects(), i))) <= 2),
           "NO OBJECT STANDS IN MORE THAN TWO ROOMS")

Def StateArityOk(o As Obj) As Boolean
    (IsEmpty(States(o)) Or IsEmpty(Descs(o))
     Or Length(Descs(o)) = Length(States(o)))

Rem ---- the vocabulary --------------------------------------------------

Def CheckVocabulary()
    Rem words are stored already cut to the five letters the parser
    Rem compares, so a six-letter synonym in the table matches nothing
    Assert(All(Motions(), Fn(v) => All(Words(v), Fn(w) => Len(w) <= TokLen())),
           "EVERY MOTION SYNONYM IS STORED CUT TO FIVE LETTERS")
    Assert(All(Actions(), Fn(v) => All(Words(v), Fn(w) => Len(w) <= TokLen())),
           "EVERY ACTION SYNONYM IS STORED CUT TO FIVE LETTERS")
    Assert(All(Objects(), Fn(o) => All(Words(o), Fn(w) => Len(w) <= TokLen())),
           "EVERY OBJECT SYNONYM IS STORED CUT TO FIVE LETTERS")

    Rem and every one of them classifies as something, which is the round
    Rem trip that matters: a word in a table the parser cannot reach is a
    Rem command nobody can type
    Assert(All(Motions(), Fn(v) => All(Words(v), Fn(w) => Known(w))),
           "EVERY MOTION SYNONYM CLASSIFIES")
    Assert(All(Objects(), Fn(o) => All(Words(o), Fn(w) => Known(w))),
           "EVERY OBJECT SYNONYM CLASSIFIES")
    Assert(All(Actions(), Fn(v) => All(Words(v), Fn(w) => Known(w))),
           "EVERY ACTION SYNONYM CLASSIFIES")

    Rem the tags are how the rules name a room, an object or a verb, so a
    Rem duplicate is a lookup that silently answers with the wrong one
    Assert(UniqueTags(Locations()), "EVERY ROOM TAG IS UNIQUE")
    Assert(UniqueTags(Objects()), "EVERY OBJECT TAG IS UNIQUE")
    Assert(UniqueTags(Motions()), "EVERY MOTION TAG IS UNIQUE")
    Assert(UniqueTags(Actions()), "EVERY ACTION TAG IS UNIQUE")

Rem The placeholder for the reservoir's magic word is deliberately not a
Rem word: the seeded one replaces it at startup.
Def Known(w As String) As Boolean
    If w = "z'zzz" Then
        True
    Else
        Not IsUnknown(Classify(w, "X'YZZ"))

Def IsUnknown(k As Kind) As Boolean
    Select Case k
        Case KUnknown
            True
        Case Else
            False

Def UniqueTags(rows As List) As Boolean
    Let tags = Map(rows, Fn(r) => Tag(r))
    All(Range(1, Length(tags)),
           Fn(i) => IndexIn(tags, 1, Length(tags), Nth(tags, i)) = i)

Rem ---- scoring and the ladders -----------------------------------------

Def CheckScoring()
    Rem the maximum is the number the game quotes at you, and it is built
    Rem from the treasure values rather than written down anywhere
    Assert(MaxScore() = 430, "THE MAXIMUM SCORE IS 430")
    Assert(MaxTreasure() = 298, "THE TREASURES ARE WORTH 298 OF IT")
    Assert(TreasureCount() = 20, "THERE ARE 20 TREASURES")

    Rem the rank ladder is read by walking it until the score fits, so an
    Rem unordered rung is a rank nobody can ever be given
    Assert(All(Range(2, Length(Classes())),
           Fn(i) => Threshold(Nth(Classes(), i)) > Threshold(Nth(Classes(), i - 1))),
           "THE RANK THRESHOLDS INCREASE")
    Assert(All(Range(2, Length(TurnThresholds())),
           Fn(i) => Threshold(Nth(TurnThresholds(), i))
                            > Threshold(Nth(TurnThresholds(), i - 1))),
           "THE TURN PENALTY THRESHOLDS INCREASE")

    Rem every rank above the bottom says something
    Assert(All(Range(2, Length(Classes())), Fn(i) => Len(Message(Nth(Classes(), i))) > 0),
           "EVERY RANK HAS SOMETHING TO SAY")

Def CheckHintTable()
    Rem a hint that costs nothing, or is offered instantly, is a hint the
    Rem game gives away
    Assert(All(Hints(), Fn(h) => Penalty(h) > 0), "EVERY HINT COSTS POINTS")
    Assert(All(Hints(), Fn(h) => Turns(h) > 0), "EVERY HINT MAKES YOU WAIT")
    Assert(All(Hints(), Fn(h) => Len(Question(h)) > 0 And Len(Text(h)) > 0),
           "EVERY HINT ASKS AND ANSWERS")

    Rem each hint is offered somewhere: a hint no room carries is dead
    Assert(All(Range(1, Length(Hints())), Fn(i) => HintIsOffered(i - 1)),
           "EVERY HINT IS OFFERED IN SOME ROOM")

Def HintIsOffered(h As Number) As Boolean
    Any(Locations(), Fn(r) => Contains(RoomHints(r), h))

Rem ---- the curmudgeons' rooms ------------------------------------------

Def CheckCurmudgeonRooms()
    Assert(All(CurmudgeonLocs(), Fn(l) => l > 0 And l < NRooms()),
           "EVERY CURMUDGEON STARTS IN A REAL ROOM")
    Rem they start deep, which is where they are allowed to walk
    Assert(All(CurmudgeonLocs(), Fn(l) => InDeep(l)),
           "EVERY CURMUDGEON STARTS DEEP IN THE CAVE")

Rem ---- can you get there from here? ------------------------------------
Rem Walking the travel table from the end of the road, ignoring every
Rem condition, answers a question no single row can: which rooms does the
Rem table not connect at all? The answer is not zero, and the rooms it
Rem names are the three places where movement deliberately escapes the
Rem table -- which is the point of the check. A fourth would be a
Rem teleport somebody added without saying so.

Def Marked(seen As Array, k As Number) As Array
    Let o = RowAt(k)
    Let s = MarkDest(seen, GoesTo(o))
    If Stop(o) Then
        s
    Else
        Marked(s, k + 1)

Def MarkDest(seen As Array, d As Number) As Array
    If d = NoRoom() Then
        seen
    Else
        SetNth(seen, d + 1, True)

Def ExpandRoom(seen As Array, loc As Number) As Array
    If Not Nth(seen, loc + 1) Then
        seen
    Else
        Let k = Nth(Tkey(), loc + 1)
        If k = 0 Then
            seen
        Else
            Marked(seen, k)

Rem An edge the travel table does not have: { from, to }.
Def ExpandEdge(seen As Array, e As List) As Array
    If Nth(seen, Nth(e, 1) + 1) Then
        SetNth(seen, Nth(e, 2) + 1, True)
    Else
        seen

Def OnePass(seen As Array, extra As List) As Array
    Let s1 = Fold(Range(0, NRooms() - 1), seen, Fn(acc, loc) => ExpandRoom(acc, loc))
    Fold(extra, s1, Fn(acc, e) => ExpandEdge(acc, e))

Def CountReached(seen As Array) As Number
    CountIf(Range(1, NRooms()), Fn(i) => Nth(seen, i))

Rem Passes until the count stops growing. A room count is a fixed point
Rem the closure cannot overshoot, so this terminates.
Def Closure(seen As Array, extra As List, before As Number) As Array
    Let next = OnePass(seen, extra)
    Let n = CountReached(next)
    If n = before Then
        next
    Else
        Closure(next, extra, n)

Def Reached(extra As List) As Array
    Closure(SetNth(Dim(NRooms(), False), 2, True), extra, 1)

Def CutOff(seen As Array) As List Of String
    Map(Filter(Range(1, NRooms()), Fn(i) => Not Nth(seen, i)),
        Fn(i) => Tag(Nth(Locations(), i)))

Def SameSet(got As List Of String, want As List Of String) As Boolean
    (Length(got) = Length(want)
     And All(got, Fn(t) => Contains(want, t)))

Rem The bridge's far side is not written in the travel table at all: the
Rem troll stands at both ends of it, and the crossing rule computes where
Rem you come out from his two placements. The rug does the same trick
Rem between the cliff and the ledge. Deriving both here the way the rules
Rem derive them means this check follows the data, not a copy of it.
Def BridgeEdges() As List
    Let ps = Places(ObjAt(ObjNamed("TROLL")))
    { { First(ps), Nth(ps, 2) }, { Nth(ps, 2), First(ps) } }

Def RugEdges() As List
    Let cliff = LocNamed("LOC_CLIFF")
    Let ledge = LocNamed("LOC_LEDGE")
    { { cliff, ledge }, { ledge, cliff } }

Def BeyondTheTable() As List Of String
    { "LOC_NE", "LOC_SW", "LOC_NECHASM", "LOC_CORRIDOR", "LOC_FORK",
      "LOC_WARMWALLS", "LOC_BREATHTAKING", "LOC_BOULDERS2", "LOC_LIMESTONE",
      "LOC_BARRENFRONT", "LOC_BARRENROOM", "LOC_LEDGE", "LOC_GRUESOME" }

Def CheckReachability()
    Rem what the rules alone connect
    Let byRules = Reached({ })
    Assert(CountReached(byRules) = 172, "172 ROOMS ARE REACHABLE BY TRAVEL RULE ALONE")
    Assert(SameSet(CutOff(byRules), BeyondTheTable()),
           "AND THE THIRTEEN THAT ARE NOT ARE THE ONES WE KNOW ABOUT")

    Rem pay the troll and nine of the thirteen open up: everything past
    Rem the chasm is on the far side of a crossing the table cannot express
    Let withBridge = Reached(BridgeEdges())
    Assert(SameSet(CutOff(withBridge), { "LOC_NE", "LOC_SW", "LOC_LEDGE" }),
           "THE TROLL BRIDGE IS THE ONLY WAY PAST THE CHASM")

    Rem the ledge is reachable only by rug
    Let withRug = Reached(Flatten({ BridgeEdges(), RugEdges() }))
    Assert(SameSet(CutOff(withRug), { "LOC_NE", "LOC_SW" }),
           "THE RUG IS THE ONLY WAY TO THE LEDGE")

    Rem and what is left is the repository, which you cannot walk into at
    Rem all: the closing sequence puts you there when the cave shuts
    Assert(Length(CutOff(withRug)) = 2, "ONLY THE REPOSITORY IS UNWALKABLE")

Def Main()
    CheckTravelRows()
    CheckTravelBlocks()
    CheckRooms()
    CheckObjects()
    CheckVocabulary()
    CheckScoring()
    CheckHintTable()
    CheckCurmudgeonRooms()
    CheckReachability()
    Print("ALL MUNGO CAVERNS TABLE CHECKS PASSED")
